{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1341839-demon-built-infrastructure","id":1341839,"title":"Demon Built Infrastructure","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-17T05:13:44-07:00","id":1341839,"title":"Demon Built Infrastructure","content":"Hey! I was just reading Night Horrors Enemy Action and the Demon Storyteller's guide. I noticed that...Demons can actually learn to use Arcane Physics themselves and build their own infrastructure. of course without the skill and power of the god machine itself, but what i wondered...is there is an actual system for this? Like i know that you have the existing systems for creating infrastructure when the st is doing it on behalf of the god machine, but if let's say the players in a game are inquistiros all pursuing the hell/path of the Arcane Physicist. I kinda would like there to be a system for that, so it doesn't fall into complete handwavium on my part.<br /> <br /> For Sources on this see page 54 in Night Horros Enemy Action and page 27 in The Demon Storytellers Guide","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T06:27:56-07:00","id":1341843,"title":"","content":"Handwavium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T09:15:38-07:00","id":1341874,"title":"","content":"boooo handwavium","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T12:18:24-07:00","id":1341916,"title":"","content":"The problem with having a system in place to make Infrastructure is that it kind of undercuts how dang <i>hard</i> the task is. Out of all the characters we know about only one is confirmed to actually be able to create Infrastructure, who has lived since the age of the Romans, has studied Infrastructure all that time, and as the text notes even then he still has problems getting a reliable output to form from years of work alongside other projects.<br /> <br /> Infrastructure is not just about knowing various arcane facts. It\u2019s about proper timing on a universal scale, knowing innate facts about the location it is being done in, and having the right materials no matter how arbitrary it may be to find/make them. That isn\u2019t to say players can\u2019t <i>eventually</i> get to a semi-similar state, but it would probably take a lot more game time and character development than most games really last/allow for, and handwaving it seems unwise.<br /> <br /> Hense the import of Handwavium. Ultimately it is up to the ST if they will allow players to make their own Infrastructure or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T13:28:39-07:00","id":1341935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1341839-demon-built-infrastructure?p=1341916#post1341916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with having a system in place to make Infrastructure is that it kind of undercuts how dang <i>hard</i> the task is. Out of all the characters we know about only one is confirmed to actually be able to create Infrastructure, who has lived since the age of the Romans, has studied Infrastructure all that time, and as the text notes even then he still has problems getting a reliable output to form from years of work alongside other projects.<br /> <br /> Infrastructure is not just about knowing various arcane facts. It\u2019s about proper timing on a universal scale, knowing innate facts about the location it is being done in, and having the right materials no matter how arbitrary it may be to find/make them. That isn\u2019t to say players can\u2019t <i>eventually</i> get to a semi-similar state, but it would probably take a lot more game time and character development than most games really last/allow for, and handwaving it seems unwise.<br /> <br /> Hense the import of Handwavium. Ultimately it is up to the ST if they will allow players to make their own Infrastructure or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>^this a lot.<br /> <br /> I <i>did</i> think for a while I was going to try and dedicate a small section of Wednesday's write-up to a basic logical setup for Arcane Physics so as to help Storytellers come up with objective points for people to contest over with Wednesday, but I ran into the problem of losing the <i>arcane</i> element of arcane physics by doing that-it should be fundamentally very weird and hard to process, with at least a minor sense of, well, sense to it, but on the other hand no one should be able to tell you how or why beating a piece of wood with a bronze bell into the shape of a frying pan during the dog days would result in you being able to use that wooden frying pan as well as anyone else.<br /> <br /> Wednesday is both old enough, broken enough, and practiced enough that, to him, there's a strong intuitive sense of how Infrastructure works-he knows it like a musician knows the math of their own compositions. Following that line of logic, a demon is going to have to develop his own intuition on the subject, as are the players <br /> <br /> If you want a good guideline, take Gadget making, add in sacred geometry, apply Infrastructure principles, and build weirdly from there. At all points in time, some major temporal factor must always feature in the accomplishment of the output.<br /> <br /> I might sit down, dig up my old notes on the subject, and whip up a way of modifying a large series of extended rolls, but for the most part, you wanna keep it special and leave it out of the realms of mechanics. This is Hell we're talking about.<br /> <br /> (as a good other guideline for figuring shit out, though, Primum, the Cipher/Pentagram, and a HUGE storehouse of Embeds goes a lot way. Wednesday should have that note pointing out that he can realistically have more than what is listed.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T02:20:30-07:00","id":1342040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1341839-demon-built-infrastructure?p=1341935#post1341935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">^this a lot.<br /> <br /> I <i>did</i> think for a while I was going to try and dedicate a small section of Wednesday's write-up to a basic logical setup for Arcane Physics so as to help Storytellers come up with objective points for people to contest over with Wednesday, but I ran into the problem of losing the <i>arcane</i> element of arcane physics by doing that-it should be fundamentally very weird and hard to process, with at least a minor sense of, well, sense to it, but on the other hand no one should be able to tell you how or why beating a piece of wood with a bronze bell into the shape of a frying pan during the dog days would result in you being able to use that wooden frying pan as well as anyone else.<br /> <br /> Wednesday is both old enough, broken enough, and practiced enough that, to him, there's a strong intuitive sense of how Infrastructure works-he knows it like a musician knows the math of their own compositions. Following that line of logic, a demon is going to have to develop his own intuition on the subject, as are the players<br /> <br /> If you want a good guideline, take Gadget making, add in sacred geometry, apply Infrastructure principles, and build weirdly from there. At all points in time, some major temporal factor must always feature in the accomplishment of the output.<br /> <br /> I might sit down, dig up my old notes on the subject, and whip up a way of modifying a large series of extended rolls, but for the most part, you wanna keep it special and leave it out of the realms of mechanics. This is Hell we're talking about.<br /> <br /> (as a good other guideline for figuring shit out, though, Primum, the Cipher/Pentagram, and a HUGE storehouse of Embeds goes a lot way. Wednesday should have that note pointing out that he can realistically have more than what is listed.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> AHA! you are the Wednesday writer, excellent. I actually had a question since it mentions in the storyhooks and his description that he can actually make his own angels. 2 questions...like how does that work. Are they constantly connected to his mind and stuff and the second question...can they fall?<br /> <br /> As for all your other points i overall agree, the thing i was more looking for was what should they roll to start working. More than anything else, i agree that a complete system for doing Arcane Physics eliminates the arcane/occult elements of it being a hidden and mysterious thing. But since we are talking about a goal that is achieveable by pcs...even if it is extremely hard. I would at least like just being told &quot;oh have them do extended rolls&quot;...which you just said in not as many words so thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T11:41:29-07:00","id":1342138,"title":"","content":"1) Intentionally, it's vague. Too much insight into how Wednesday's angels work is insight into how normal angels work, and since that should be one of the big mysteries of the G-M since that can be used against It in big ways, I didn't answer it too much beyond pointing out that we know how angels operate.<br /> <br /> Now one thing worth noting is that Wednesday doesn't have the personal infrastructure to do everything the G-M does, so a lot of the instant update of information that angels are privvy to for minor information isn't quite there-but that said, it seems reasonable that angels are able to pick up on his knowledge base concerning their mission. In as much as the G-M relies on Messengers as well for angels, at times, Wednesday also relies on Messenger Imperatives-I'll say now that Messenger and Analyst Imperatives are a relatively easy Output (which does not mean it's actually easy, but Wednesday can reliably pull them off.) Now, whether he is always aware of what they are doing or needs to do things the old fashioned way while the angels need updates, that's up to the storyteller.<br /> <br /> The best way to think of it is that Wednesday is a small scale G-M, with the main disadvantage of being that while the God-Machine is the sum total of Infrastructure in existence, Wednesday the Demon is very much a central brain unit for the &quot;Wednesday-Machine&quot;-while he is very much the sum total of his own infrastructure, you put a bullet in his head, it all does go down.<br /> <br /> That doesn't have to always be the case, though.<br /> <br /> 2) Yep! Wednesday's Angels can Fall! We sort of assumed that would be assumed.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, we didn't think about the implications of that all the way through, because space and time are concerns. Regarding his angels, he has a benefit and a curse-because Wednesday isn't as rigid in his missions, there's a lot of normal circumstances where an angel would Fall but doesn't-but because he's not as rigid in his missions, there's actually a lot of new ways they can Fall, and a hell of lot more where they can wander off into Abandonment.<br /> <br /> His primary answer to this leads into the above situation-he tries to avoid creating the sort of situations where Falling will happen, and he uses his latitude that the G-M doesn't demonstrate to cover unexpected scenarios. It's a good way to explore how the G-M became the way it did.<br /> <br /> One way he is instantly like the G-M though is his response to Falls and Abandonment-while he plans long and therefore this needs to be understood in that context-as soon as that hole in his knowledge is formed, he starts to prioritze a plan to kill them. Sometimes that involves getting them to rely on as much of sense of safety in demonic society as can be managed before assassinating them, sometimes that involves taking advantage of the difference of experience to alienate and isolate the demon, and sometimes that involves dropping plans for the evening and hunting down the thing himself, but Wednesday tolerates misbehaving equipment <i>less</i> than the God-machine does. If enough of his angels fell to have Agendas regarding him, Turncoats would notably be rarer.<br /> <br /> Worth noting is that Wednesday is also like the G-M in that he is very sparing in terms of making angels.The world is lousy with angels because the G-M has had the whole of human history and Not Failing As Bad As Wednesday Has (Hercules once squared off with him and Cacus-the story that humanity got is heavily truncated for [reasons])-meanwhile, Wednesday may be millenia old, but he doen't have the benefit of possibly having been around since time began, and he has often stumbled into an all too human problem of putting all his eggs in one Spear of Destiny and having it blow up in his face(weird metaphor is weird) due to emotion, acknowledgement of mortality, all the usual reasons, and of course it took him a long time to know how to do this(how long is up to the G-M, don't let me tell you you can't have Wednesday in the Sundered World making angels), so he doesn't have all the infrastructure in the world to churn things out. But Once you get around the volume comparison, he tends to make angels when he is <i>very sure</i> it's the right answer for the job and <i>very sure</i> the chances of Falling or Abandonment are minimal, particularly under a good set of parameters. Again, like the G-M.<br /> <br /> Now regarding the fun question here, what would it mean to be a Wednesday Demon?<br /> <br /> My central argument is that early on, it's freeing and at the same time limiting. His demons are still plugged into the network, so to speak, but at a remove, so compromise rolls inherently have a +3 bonus to them against the normal God-Machine (if you don't get a success, roll the three to see if Wednesday notices). On the other hand, Embeds are more limited to get a hold of. Any Mundane Embed can be gotten, but Storyteller's should probably figure out with the player which half of Cacophonic and Instrumental Embeds are missing, and be creatively minimal with Vocal. This lasts until the Demon is Primum 3 or 4, at which point the demon has asserted enough self-identity that they also plug properly into the wider G-M's network-though Wednesday may still be aware of them until they do something to seperate themselves completely from his infrastructural awareness, if such is possible.<br /> <br /> Ciphers and Keys should be weird, and I would argue any Key obtained before the Primum rise asides from the Initial key should muddle with the entire affair, resulting in glitched Ciphers and off-beat Interlocks(even for Interlocks). If a Demon is properly plugged into the wider network, performing the Pentagram may &quot;fix&quot; things in as much as it &quot;fixes&quot; anything. The ideal, though, would be to not start on the Cipher until the Demon is freed up, as if any demon is going to do that.<br /> <br /> The large point is that Wednesday is a Cosmic-tier antagonist because it gives your players a real angle to learn things about the God-Machine, as well as to explore what a more human like God-Machine would be like (and why that would be terrifying), and what happens when Gods collide. Players should get an opportunity to love him, fear him, and ultimately dread, defy, and end him, because his role is to microcosmically compare and contrast with the God-machine.<br /> <br /> And beyond all of that, the large point of Wednesday is that he is a broken person who's stuck in his own cycle and is doing the best he can to do what he thinks is right-and maybe, underneath all of that, fix the holes in himself. He should be allowed to show himself as silly and liking to be around people, he should be allowed to show fear and remorse over losing his memories and loved ones-and he should <i>absolutely</i> be allowed to show how he turns all of that into fuel for cold calculation that plays over centuries, steel-hearted sacrifices that cut down anyone unessential, and arcane humanism that will ascend the masses into terrible nightmares.<br /> <br /> He's a broken person who is <i>far</i> too good at playing God-Machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-18-2019, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T03:26:50-07:00","id":1342318,"title":"","content":"thanks for a very long and informative answer <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. The reason i asked, is because i am always interested in plots with lesser g-ms or competing creatures that seeks to become like it. Like that promethean thing mentioned in the contagion chronicle, or the plot hook in the demon st guide for an indigam getting merged with infrastructure and trying to become a new god machine itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T22:49:39-07:00","id":1400636,"title":"","content":"Apologies if this is thread necromancy, but my best suggestion for handling demon made infrastructure is to look at the rules of &quot;mortal interaction&quot; and look at how a fair bit of it seems to overlap with some descriptions of infrastructure. Not all of it of course but enough for it to be a starting point. The GM exploits the rules of reality so the starting point of mimicing what the machine can build is to look for the rules that it has built itself upon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}